{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:(19439893 OR 32317131) AND SRC:MED AND OPEN_ACCESS:y","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":1000,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"32317131","source":"MED","pmid":"32317131","pmcid":"PMC7253896","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC7253896"]},"doi":"10.1016/j.abd.2020.02.001","title":"Post-finasteride syndrome.","authorString":"Pereira AFJR, Coelho TOA.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Pereira AFJR","lastName":"Pereira","firstName":"Ana Francisca Junqueira Ribeiro","initials":"AFJR","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Trichology Outpatient Clinic, Dermatology Service, Hospital das Clínicas, Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais, Belo Horizonte, MG, Brazil. Electronic address: anafranciscadermato@gmail.com."}]}},{"fullName":"Coelho TOA","lastName":"Coelho","firstName":"Thaissa Oliveira de Almeida","initials":"TOA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Trichology Outpatient Clinic, Dermatology Service, Hospital das Clínicas, Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais, Belo Horizonte, MG, Brazil."}]}}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"95","journalIssueId":2958721,"dateOfPublication":"2020 May - Jun","monthOfPublication":0,"yearOfPublication":2020,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"An Bras Dermatol","title":"Anais brasileiros de dermatologia","essn":"1806-4841","issn":"0365-0596","nlmid":"0067662","isoabbreviation":"An Bras Dermatol"},"printPublicationDate":"2020-05-01"},"pubYear":"2020","pageInfo":"271-277","abstractText":"Finasteride is a 5α-reductase enzyme inhibitor that has been approved for the treatment of male androgenic alopecia since 1997. Over time, it has been considered a safe and well-tolerated drug with rare and reversible side effects. Recently there have been reports of adverse drug-related reactions that persisted for at least three months after discontinuation of this drug, and the term post-finasteride syndrome arose. It includes persistent sexual, neuropsychiatric, and physical symptoms. Studies to date cannot refute or confirm this syndrome as a nosological entity. If it actually exists, it seems to occur in susceptible people, even if exposed to small doses and for short periods, and symptoms may persist for long periods. Based on currently available data, the use of 5α-reductase inhibitors in patients with a history of depression, sexual dysfunction, or infertility should be carefully and individually assessed.","affiliation":"Trichology Outpatient Clinic, Dermatology Service, Hospital das Clínicas, Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais, Belo Horizonte, MG, Brazil. Electronic address: anafranciscadermato@gmail.com.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Spermatozoa","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Infertility","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cardiovascular Diseases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Metabolic Diseases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Syndrome"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Finasteride","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ris